---
import Cmd from "../../components/Cmd.astro";
import DocsNode from "../../layouts/DocsNode.astro";
---

<DocsNode
	slug="getting-started"
	description="Build and run Floodgate locally with gleam run, or as a container with docker compose."
>
	<p>
		Floodgate refuses to start without an explicit JWT secret — there is no
		default that would quietly leave a deployment unauthenticated.
	</p>

	<h2 class="rule-label">run directly</h2>
	<Cmd command="FLOODGATE_JWT_SECRET=dev-secret gleam run" />

	<h2 class="rule-label">or as a container</h2>
	<Cmd command="docker compose up -d --wait" />
	<p class="note">starts on http://localhost:3000</p>
	<Cmd command="docker compose logs -f floodgate" />
	<p class="note">follow the server log</p>
	<Cmd command="docker compose down -v" />
	<p class="note">stop and remove the data volume</p>

	<p>
		<code>FLOODGATE_JWT_SECRET</code> also seeds the startup tenant
		(<code>FLOODGATE_TENANT_ID</code>, default <code>fluid</code>) with that
		value as its first secret slot — see{" "}
		<a href="/docs/multi-tenancy">Multi-tenancy</a> for what that tenant can
		do beyond boot. Once it's up, <code>GET /health</code> answers{" "}
		<code>{`{"status":"ok"}`}</code>, and the full set of knobs for the
		listen address, storage backend, and connection limits lives in{" "}
		<a href="/docs/configuration">Configuration</a>.
	</p>
</DocsNode>
